   read B1.h
      now  legal (one, B:A's h)
      A0   ERROR: `B1.h`: `h` is not visible through `B1` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A    ERROR: `B1.h`: `h` is not visible through `B1` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A2   legal (one, B:A's h)
      B    ERROR: `B1.h`: `h` is not visible through `B1` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
   read B1.p.h
      now  legal (one, B:A's h)
      A0   ERROR: `B1.p.h`: `p.h` is not visible through `B1` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A    ERROR: `B1.p.h`: `p.h` is not visible through `B1` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A2   legal (one, B:A's h)
      B    ERROR: `B1.p.h`: `p.h` is not visible through `B1` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
   read B1.p
      now  legal (one, B:B1's p)
      A0   legal (one, B:B1's p)
      A    legal (one, B:B1's p)
      A2   legal (one, B:B1's p)
      B    legal (one, B:B1's p)
   RUN B1.h reads A's h (the list passes the part [p = rx]'s labels):
