   hand: the walker does not parse label parameters. Reading (i): x is the sender's own name, so x.h and x.p.h are legal (route 3). Reading (ii): the path from x crosses the body's p and then the argument's place, so x.p.h (and x.h, which skips p) go THROUGH the place: errors. Today: legal (the sent label is a start, one-path skips p)
