      A2   ERROR: `n.d`: a `d` sits behind a gate (a part used alone is never skipped): write the full path, `n.L1.d` or `n.P.d` (a compile error, core/labels/rule/paths rule 4, one-path)
      B    ERROR: `n.d`: a `d` sits behind a gate (a part used alone is never skipped): write the full path, `n.L1.d` or `n.P.d` (a compile error, core/labels/rule/paths rule 4, one-path)
   read n.L1.d
      now  legal (one, B:Q's d)
      A0   legal (one, B:Q's d)
      A    legal (one, B:Q's d)
      A2   legal (one, B:Q's d)
      B    legal (one, B:Q's d)
   RUN n.L1.d, Q's d:
      WHOLE `7,3` HOLDS, `3,7` FAILS / SEARCHED `3,7 7,3` `7,3`@4 / FIND-ALL `7,3 3,7 1,2` [`7,3`@0, `1,2`@8]
      (regex (?P<g2>(?:(?:(?P<g0>\d))(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:,(?P<g1>[0-4])))))))))

== index: metadata of a label inside an argument, and of the body's own label on the place
   program `[c = Bm(A)] & (c.a.h: <5)`, A := /(?<h>\d)/; Bm(x) := [a = x] | [b = /z/]
   read c.a.h
      now  legal (one, B:A's h)
      A0   ERROR: `c.a.h`: `a.h` is not visible through `c` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A    ERROR: `c.a.h`: `a.h` is not visible through `c` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A2   ERROR: `c.a.h`: `a.h` is not visible through `c` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      B    ERROR: `c.a.h`: `a.h` is not visible through `c` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
   read c.a
      now  legal (one, B:Bm's a)
      A0   legal (one, B:Bm's a)
      A    legal (one, B:Bm's a)
      A2   legal (one, B:Bm's a)
      B    legal (one, B:Bm's a)
   hand: `(c.a.index: 1)` (the body's own label's metadata, a path that ends on the place) and `(c.b.index: 2)` stay legal; `c.a.h` and any metadata below it (`c.a.h.index` where h sits under a member) go through the place
   RUN A.h:
      WHOLE `3` HOLDS, `z` FAILS, `7` FAILS / SEARCHED `7 z 3` `3`@4 / FIND-ALL `3 z 7 4` [`3`@0, `4`@6]
      (regex (?P<g3>(?:(?:(?P<g1>(?:(?:(?P<g0>[0-4]))))|(?P<g2>z)))))

== capture: a capture request for an argument's label
   program `B(A) & (B.h: <5)`, A := /(?<h>\d)/; B(rx) := /${[p = rx]}xx/
   read B.h
      now  legal (one, B:A's h)
      A0   ERROR: `B.h`: `h` is not visible through `B` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A    ERROR: `B.h`: `h` is not visible through `B` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A2   ERROR: `B.h`: `h` is not visible through `B` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      B    ERROR: `B.h`: `h` is not visible through `B` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
   hand: `B(A) & (B.h: capture("h"))` is route (1): an error under the candidate (the path is the read's, lib/structural/capture: "the label is named where conditions name labels, by its path"); `(A.h: capture("h"))` and, through a list, `identity(A) & (identity.h: capture("h"))` stay

== when-shape: when's then branch: test and then both set h (the shape W of the library)
   program `W(/(?<h>\d)/, /;(?<h>\d)/) & (W.h: <5)`, W(a, b) := [(=) = a] SEQ [(=) = b]
   read W.h
      now  ERROR: `W.h`: 2 labels `h` are visible from `W`, so no step may be skipped: no path from `W` names one of them alone (a compile error, core/labels/rule/paths rule 4, one-path)
      A0   ERROR: `W.h`: 2 labels `h` are visible from `W`, so no step may be skipped: no path from `W` names one of them alone (a compile error, core/labels/rule/paths rule 4, one-path)
      A    ERROR: `W.h`: 2 labels `h` are visible from `W`, so no step may be skipped: no path from `W` names one of them alone (a compile error, core/labels/rule/paths rule 4, one-path)
      A2   ERROR: `W.h`: 2 labels `h` are visible from `W`, so no step may be skipped: no path from `W` names one of them alone (a compile error, core/labels/rule/paths rule 4, one-path)
      B    legal (last mention, P's h)
   RUN the last mention, then's h (reading B: the listed labels are the body's own):
      WHOLE `7;3` HOLDS, `3;7` FAILS / SEARCHED `3;7 7;3` `7;3`@4 / FIND-ALL `7;3 3;7 1;2` [`7;3`@0, `1;2`@8]
      (regex (?:(?:(?:(?P<g0>\d)))(?:(?:;(?P<g1>[0-4])))))

== map: a map built by a macro from its arguments (as a pattern: labelled alternatives)
   program `[m = Mk(A, Z)] & (m.a.h: <5)`, A := /(?<h>\d)/; Z := /z/; Mk(x, y) := [a = x] | [b = y]
   read m.a.h
      now  legal (one, B:A's h)
      A0   ERROR: `m.a.h`: `a.h` is not visible through `m` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A    ERROR: `m.a.h`: `a.h` is not visible through `m` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A2   ERROR: `m.a.h`: `a.h` is not visible through `m` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      B    ERROR: `m.a.h`: `a.h` is not visible through `m` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
   read m.a
      now  legal (one, B:Mk's a)
      A0   legal (one, B:Mk's a)
      A    legal (one, B:Mk's a)
      A2   legal (one, B:Mk's a)
      B    legal (one, B:Mk's a)
   hand: a module's members are reached by `.`; a member a macro builds on an argument (`{a = x}`) is the body's own label on the place: `m.a` stays, `m.a.h` is route (1); `{a = [(=) = x]}` would be the carve-out
   RUN A.h:
      WHOLE `3` HOLDS, `z` FAILS, `7` FAILS / SEARCHED `7 z 3` `3`@4 / FIND-ALL `3 z 7 4` [`3`@0, `4`@6]
      (regex (?P<g3>(?:(?:(?P<g1>(?:(?:(?P<g0>[0-4]))))|(?P<g2>(?:(?:z)))))))

== own-then-listed: unpredictability: the body's own d BEFORE the listed place
   program `Bo(Ad) & (Bo.d: <5)`, Ad := /(?<d>\d)/; Bo(rx) := /(?<d>\d)-${[(=) = rx]}/
   read Bo.d
