      A    ERROR: `Y.c.h`: `c.h` is not visible through `Y` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      A2   ERROR: `Y.c.h`: `c.h` is not visible through `Y` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
      B    ERROR: `Y.c.h`: `c.h` is not visible through `Y` (a compile error, core/labels/paths)
   hand: reading (i): Y's text writes `a`, and a binding exports the labels its own text writes (export statement 3), so Y.a.h is legal; reading (ii): the path Y, B, p, the place, a crosses B's place: an error, and then a caller's label in an argument never leaves the caller
   RUN A's h:
      WHOLE `3xx!` HOLDS, `7xx!` FAILS / SEARCHED `7xx! 3xx!` `3xx!`@5 / FIND-ALL `3xx! 7xx! 4xx!` [`3xx!`@0, `4xx!`@10]
